WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.439
To test whether annotators really matter,

00:00:02.519 --> 00:00:08.093
the authors randomly shuffle which annotator mask
is attached to each of the eighty thousand

00:00:08.173 --> 00:00:11.411
judgments and recompute accuracy a hundred times over.

00:00:11.491 --> 00:00:16.327
Accuracy drops from about sixty-two percent down to
roughly fifty-three percent,

00:00:16.407 --> 00:00:19.891
proving that annotators are genuinely not interchangeable.

00:00:19.971 --> 00:00:25.237
A dimension-elimination analysis further shows that
only six to thirteen dimensions are

00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:28.310
needed to recover most of the predictive accuracy,

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:34.025
while fifteen to twenty-two dimensions are required
to explain the full similarity structure,

00:00:34.105 --> 00:00:37.220
clear evidence that similarity is context-dependent.
